"""Preparation-only oracle for the FlagGems ``_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward``.

This file is the reference-as-solution artifact, not an optimized candidate and
not a numerical claim.  It is injected through the existing FlagGems pytest
protocol only:

    --override _upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward:<this file>:run

``flag_gems.cli_override.apply_overrides_from_args`` ->
``dynamic_registry.DynamicOpOverride.override_from_file`` does
``setattr(flag_gems, "_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward", wrapper)``, so the
public attribute that the frozen suites call (master
``tests/test_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward.py`` lines 50/71/89) is replaced
by ``run``.  ``torch.ops.aten`` keeps dispatching to native ATen because the
override only rebinds a Python attribute and never enables ``use_gems()``.

Faithfulness notes
------------------
* The frozen cases compute their expected value with
  ``torch.ops.aten._upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward.default(grad_output,
  output_size, input_size, *scales)`` (master test lines 41-49, 68-70, 86-88),
  so ``run`` delegates to that very operator with the same positional
  ``(scales_d, scales_h, scales_w)`` arguments, which may be ``None`` or the
  explicit float triple (``(0.6, 1.75, 8/3)``, ``(1.5, 2.5, 0.75)``,
  ``(None, 1.0, -1.0)``).  Non-positive/absent scales keep the native
  ``output_size/input_size`` fallback instead of being re-derived here.
* Return contract comes from ``definitions/_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward.json``
  (``outputs: ["out"]``, ``effects.mutates: []``,
  ``effects.returns_alias_of: {}``): a new tensor with ``grad_output``'s dtype
  and device and ``input_size`` shape, produced without writing into
  ``grad_output``; a non-contiguous ``grad_output`` stays untouched and native
  stride handling is preserved (master test lines 82-92).
* Only ``torch`` is imported: the oracle never imports ``flag_gems``, never
  reads the replaced export and never runs the frozen Triton kernel, so it is
  not its own oracle and cannot re-enter the overridden callable.

The sibling out overload (``_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward_grad_input``,
``definitions/_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward_grad_input.json``) is a
different public export with a different ``--override`` key; the one-key-per-
phase review protocol cannot inject both, so it is deliberately not declared in
``review-manifest.json`` (see ``source_alignment_notes`` there) rather than being
run un-injected or exercised through an out-of-band side effect here.
"""

import torch


def run(
    grad_output,
    output_size,
    input_size,
    scales_d=None,
    scales_h=None,
    scales_w=None,
):
    """Native ATen reference for the non-out ``_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward``."""
    return torch.ops.aten._upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward.default(
        grad_output,
        output_size,
        input_size,
        scales_d,
        scales_h,
        scales_w,
    )
